| `scripts/model_budget.py` | Holds an agent `--execute` run to the approved model-call cap before any model is built (`cap`, `approve`, which raises `SpendRefused` for a bound over the cap or a bound it cannot read), names the registry default a run with no `--model` will use (`announce`), and words the failure of a run stopped at its count (`stopped`). | imported by `scripts/doc_review.py`, `scripts/refactor_practice.py` and the two Stop hooks | [`agents.max_model_calls`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Judges the run's bound before it starts; the count of calls made is `models.CountedModel`'s, which stops the run at that bound. Never ends the process: each CLI turns `SpendRefused` into exit 2 and a stopped run into exit 1. Not the eval harness's cap: `evals.live.max_calls` is. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
